    "stdout_tail": "{\"type\":\"result\",\"subtype\":\"success\",\"is_error\":false,\"api_error_status\":null,\"duration_ms\":174027,\"duration_api_ms\":154334,\"ttft_ms\":2035,\"ttft_stream_ms\":1615,\"time_to_request_ms\":119,\"num_turns\":25,\"result\":\"All 32 tests pass. Here's a summary of what changed and how it was validated:\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n**What changed:** `internal/cli/export.go`, `BranchesFor` method (line 1478).\\n\\n**The bug:** When a checkpoint was originally recorded on a feature branch and later merged into the default branch, `BranchesFor` returned the feature branch unconditionally (because `metadataBranch != \\\"\\\"`), filing the transcript under the old feature-branch folder instead of the default-branch folder.\\n\\n**The fix:** Moved the `DefaultCheckpointIDs` reachability check to the top of `BranchesFor`. Now, if the checkpoint is reachable from the default branch (proven by `buildCheckpointBranchDestinations` scanning the default branch's git log), it is grouped under the default branch regardless of what the metadata's `branch` field says. The original branch is still preserved in `SourceBranch` via `addSelectedSession`, so the provenance is retained.\\n\\n**Validation commands that passed:**\\n- `go test ./internal/cli/ -run \\\"TestSnapshotMetadata|TestExportSelectsLatest|TestBuildBranch|TestExportUses|TestExportDebug\\\"` \u2014 all 8 targeted tests pass\\n- `go test ./internal/cli/ -run \\\"Export|Snapshot|Branch|Checkpoint|checkpoint\\\"` \u2014 all 32 relevant tests pass\",\"stop_reason\":\"end_turn\",\"session_id\":\"f332da85-c283-4274-ad84-4e62ea9da7aa\",\"total_cost_usd\":1.0690665,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":26,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":74644,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":1694115,\"output_tokens\":7526,\"server_tool_use\":{\"web_search_requests\":0,\"web_fetch_requests\":0},\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":74644,\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0},\"inference_geo\":